Mugen Morph Workflow
Mugen Morph’s existing product materials include an audio-driven animation workflow powered by a cloud API, as well as an Unreal Engine plugin and a Unity sample project. This preview focuses on an image-and-audio-driven character expression workflow, highlighting how an emotion setting affects the resulting facial performance.
The demo workflow:
1. Upload a character image.
2. Provide or upload an audio clip.
3. Select an emotion.
4. Generate the character’s facial performance for presentation on a Mesh, in video, or as a 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) character.
Example Use Cases
Image- and audio-driven character expressions can support a range of content workflows, including:
- Digital presenters: Add a character presenter to a course slide, presentation, or explainer video.
- Courses and educational content: Create character-led lessons, training materials, and knowledge-sharing content.
- Character performance previews: Compare how one character performs with different emotion settings.
- Creator content: Combine a character image and audio to create expressive character-led content.
